Hi Ruchi,

Thank you for your email and for sharing the details of the discussion.

I would like to respectfully clarify a few points from my understanding 
of our conversation, so that there is no misunderstanding and we are 
aligned regarding the next steps.

Regarding the statement that I was aware of the possible course of 
action and had accordingly been evaluating my future plans, my 
understanding was that I was aware of the current employment situation 
within the organization, including the reduction in workforce over time. 
Considering the uncertainty around the situation, I had started thinking 
about my future plans and evaluating different possibilities.

Regarding the reference to *two offers in hand*, I would like to clarify 
that I had shared two possible options that I was considering, rather 
than two confirmed offers. One option was to explore my personal 
business plans, while the other was to explore a potential new 
employment opportunity. I may have mentioned that I was evaluating these 
options, but my intention was not to communicate that I had two 
confirmed offers in hand.

Regarding the statement that I had indicated that I do not foresee a 
continued association with the organization, I would like to clarify the 
context of our discussion. At the beginning of the meeting, I was 
informed that the company was considering a *30-day separation/notice 
period*. This was unexpected information for me, and the discussion 
regarding my future plans and transition took place after this 
information was shared with me.

Therefore, I would appreciate it if my comments regarding my future 
plans could be understood in the context of the discussion and 
information shared during that meeting.

Regarding the employment documents, I would be happy to review the 
applicable documents and terms. I would appreciate it if the relevant 
documents could be shared with me over email, so that I can review them 
and ensure that my understanding is aligned with the applicable 
employment terms.

Before we proceed with the handover and finalize my last working day, I 
would also appreciate your clarification regarding the notice period 
applicable to my employment, as I currently have some uncertainty due to 
the following:

During our meeting, I understood that the company was providing a 
*30-day separation/notice period*.
As per my understanding, my appointment letter mentions a *45-day notice 
period*.
During my last appraisal, I recall signing an agreement/document that 
mentioned a *90-day notice period*.

Could you please confirm which notice period is applicable in my case 
and, if possible, share the relevant document/agreement for my reference?

Once the applicable notice period and terms are confirmed, I will be 
able to align accordingly on the handover requirements and last working 
date.

I appreciate your support and understanding. I remain committed to 
ensuring a professional and smooth transition and will fully cooperate 
with the required handover process.

Regards,
Rahul

